{
  "id": "delete-operation-for-two-strings",
  "questionId": "delete-operation-for-two-strings",
  "slug": "delete-operation-for-two-strings",
  "title": "Delete Operation for Two Strings",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Dp 2d",
  "patterns": [
    "dynamic programming",
    "strings"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "whatever characters remain after deleting the minimum number from both strings must form a common subsequence of the two - and to minimize deletions, you want to keep as much as possible",
    "so the real question becomes: what's the longest common subsequence (LCS) between word1 and word2? every character not in that LCS must be deleted from its string",
    "define dp[i][j] as the length of the LCS between the first i characters of word1 and the first j characters of word2, using the standard LCS recurrence",
    "once you have the LCS length L, the answer is (word1.length - L) + (word2.length - L), since those are exactly the characters in each string that aren't part of the shared subsequence",
    "fill the LCS table with dp[i][j] = 1 + dp[i-1][j-1] when characters match, else max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1]), then apply the deletion formula"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "trying to directly define a 'deletions' DP from scratch instead of recognizing this reduces cleanly to longest common subsequence",
    "forgetting to subtract the LCS length from BOTH string lengths, only accounting for deletions from one side",
    "off-by-one errors in the standard LCS table indexing"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two strings, `word1` and `word2`.\n\n**Find the minimum total number of characters you must delete, from either string, one at a time, so that the two strings become identical.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= word1.length, word2.length <= 500",
      "words consist of lowercase English letters"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "the two strings are already identical (zero deletions needed)",
      "the two strings share no characters at all (delete everything from both)",
      "one string is a subsequence of the other"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
